{"abstract":[{"text":"The score-instrument type represents a single instrument within a score-part. As with the score-part type,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each score-instrument has a required ID attribute, a name, and an optional abbreviation.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLScoreInstrumentV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLScoreInstrument","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLScoreInstrument","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLScoreInstrument"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLScoreInstrument","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLScoreInstrument"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A score-instrument type is also required if the score specifies MIDI 1.0 channels, banks, or programs. An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"initial midi-instrument assignment can also be made here. MusicXML software should be able to automatically"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"assign reasonable channels and instruments without these elements in simple cases, such as where part names"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"match General MIDI instrument names."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The score-instrument element can also distinguish multiple instruments of the same type that are on the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"part, such as Clarinet 1 and Clarinet 2 instruments within a Cl